{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never completes: recv_buf_valid stays 0 instead of 1, causing uart timeout with no byte received. In recv_state 10 completion the code assigns recv_buf_valid <= 2 which truncates to 0 for a 1-bit valid flag. Thus recv_buf_data is captured from recv_pattern but never marked valid.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
 				10: begin
 					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
-						recv_buf_valid <= 2;
+						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, loopback 0xa5 received with no uart timeout"}

